{"title":"Number of Ways to Reorder Array to Get Same BST","difficulty":"Hard","statement":"You are given a permutation `nums` of the integers `1` to `n`. Inserting its elements one by one, from left to right, into an initially empty binary search tree (smaller values go to the left subtree, larger values to the right subtree) produces a particular tree shape.\n\nCount how many **other** orderings of the same `n` numbers would produce exactly the same tree, shape and values included. The original ordering itself is **not** counted.\n\nFor example, for `[2, 3, 1]` the tree has `2` at the root, `1` on its left and `3` on its right. The ordering `[2, 1, 3]` builds the same tree, and no other ordering does, so the answer is `1`.\n\nThe answer can be large, so print it modulo `1000000007` (`10^9 + 7`).","inputFormat":"The first line contains the integer `n`.\nThe second line contains `n` space-separated integers: the permutation `nums`.","outputFormat":"Print a single integer: the number of other orderings that build the same BST, modulo `1000000007`.","constraints":["1 ≤ n ≤ 1000","`nums` is a permutation of `1..n`","The tree built from `nums` has depth at most 1000, so a recursive solution stays within the recursion limits"],"examples":[{"input":"3\n2 3 1","output":"1","explanation":"Value 2 is the root, 1 goes left and 3 goes right. Only the order of 1 and 3 is free, and swapping them gives the other ordering `[2, 1, 3]`, so there is exactly 1 other way."},{"input":"5\n3 4 5 1 2","output":"5","explanation":"The root is 3. The left side holds `1, 2` and the right side holds `4, 5`, each in a fixed internal order. Choosing which 2 of the 4 later positions belong to the left side gives `C(4, 2) = 6` interleavings, including the original order, so the answer is 6 - 1 = 5."},{"input":"3\n1 2 3","output":"0","explanation":"Every element goes to the right of the previous one, so the root must come first, then 2, then 3. No other ordering builds this tree."}],"tests":[{"input":"1\n1","output":"0"},{"input":"2\n1 2","output":"0"},{"input":"2\n2 1","output":"0"},{"input":"3\n2 1 3","output":"1"},{"input":"3\n3 2 1","output":"0"},{"input":"7\n4 2 6 1 3 5 7","output":"79"},{"input":"3\n1 3 2","output":"0"},{"input":"4\n3 4 2 1","output":"2"},{"input":"4\n3 2 4 1","output":"2"},{"input":"4\n2 4 3 1","output":"2"},{"input":"4\n4 3 1 2","output":"0"},{"input":"5\n3 4 5 2 1","output":"5"},{"input":"5\n3 1 2 5 4","output":"5"},{"input":"5\n3 5 2 1 4","output":"5"},{"input":"5\n2 4 3 5 1","output":"7"},{"input":"6\n3 1 5 6 2 4","output":"19"},{"input":"6\n4 6 1 2 5 3","output":"9"},{"input":"6\n4 5 6 2 1 3","output":"19"},{"input":"6\n6 5 3 1 2 4","output":"2"},{"input":"7\n2 1 3 4 7 6 5","output":"5"},{"input":"7\n7 3 1 5 4 2 6","output":"19"},{"input":"7\n1 5 2 6 7 4 3","output":"9"},{"input":"7\n6 3 1 5 2 4 7","output":"35"},{"input":"8\n3 7 8 2 5 6 1 4","output":"167"},{"input":"8\n7 5 3 4 2 6 8 1","output":"104"},{"input":"8\n6 4 2 5 7 1 8 3","output":"167"},{"input":"8\n1 3 7 4 2 6 5 8","output":"23"},{"input":"7\n1 2 3 4 5 6 7","output":"0"},{"input":"1000\n495 565 433 203 220 591 849 788 793 829 489 442 826 766 837 227 936 193 248 820 980 972 596 840 543 637 818 128 144 628 255 259 45 42 615 33 623 359 485 102 984 879 148 687 975 998 352 88 131 48 866 658 832 606 908 142 701 536 625 720 35 93 32 743 479 121 661 451 836 230 634 70 161 270 376 137 714 59 683 140 763 963 492 757 875 136 214 149 106 590 545 790 200 754 420 887 662 657 263 557 419 934 673 295 722 730 169 383 509 309 294 156 916 967 181 575 323 902 781 713 85 711 621 944 647 470 659 21 855 577 794 759 167 511 351 234 384 704 816 608 703 321 684 151 18 381 393 457 216 339 297 385 999 560 581 526 190 508 484 748 160 524 556 878 939 317 989 250 694 454 551 247 399 237 249 232 17 324 698 91 475 896 948 780 184 639 13 996 207 414 244 335 955 604 115 932 29 922 589 116 522 594 341 976 223 877 10 394 671 942 776 206 965 537 620 979 931 585 326 770 609 236 267 762 374 632 68 293 191 34